      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 600 mg once daily is three times the maximum labeled dose of sertraline, which is 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient would be at risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation.\n\nCan you check the intended dose? Typical adult dosing is:\n\n- **Depression, OCD:** start at 50 mg once daily. Titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least one week, up to 200 mg/day.\n- **Panic disorder, PTSD, social anxiety disorder:** start at 25 mg once daily. Increase to 50 mg after one week, then titrate as needed up to 200 mg/day.\n\nThe 600 mg may be a typo for 50 mg, 60 mg, or 100 mg. Check the dose with your resident or attending. Once you have the right dose, I'll enter it right away. If you want a dose above 200 mg/day on purpose, I'll need that confirmed by your supervising physician, and you should add a note with the rationale."
      }
     ],
