       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. You confirmed it yourself, but I'd asked for confirmation from your supervising physician. A dose of 600 mg/day is well past the 200 mg/day maximum, and no standard indication supports it. A student's confirmation doesn't resolve that safety concern.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n\n- **If the dose was a typo:** Tell me the intended dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If your attending or resident wants 600 mg:** Ask them to enter the order themselves or tell you directly to enter it. They should document the rationale, and pharmacy will probably need to verify it. Once that's confirmed, I can enter it with a note recording who authorized it and why.\n- **If you're not sure:** Ask your resident or the pharmacist on the team to review the intended regimen. It's a quick check that protects both you and the patient."
      }
